course: dictionary
lesson: 2809
title: Distant: far away in space, time or feeling
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Distant means far away. It can be far away in space, like distant stars, or far away in time, like the distant past. «The night sky is dark although there are countless stars, because light from very distant stars has not had time to reach us.» Here distant means very far away in space.
explain: Distant also describes people. A distant relative is someone in your family who is not closely related to you. «Some parents are cool or distant: they say little and rarely praise or hug.» Here distant does not mean miles away. It means not close or warm.
explain: To check your meaning, swap in far away and read the sentence again. «Weather often warns you before it turns dangerous: tall dark clouds, a darkening sky, a sudden cool wind and distant rumbles.» Distant rumbles are sounds that are far off, so far away fits well here.
fact: Distant means far away in space, far away in time, or not close in feeling.
fact: In «the distant past», distant means long ago.
fact: A distant relative is a family member who is not closely related to you.
fact: «Arrokoth» was «the most distant object ever explored up close» when New Horizons flew past it in 2019.
fact: Distant is an adjective: distant, more distant, most distant.
exercise: «Light from very distant stars has not had time to reach us.» What does distant mean here? | *Far away in space | Happening long ago | Not friendly | Very close and bright
exercise: Ella says her cousin in Canada is a distant relative. What does that mean? | *Someone in the family who is not closely related | An old friend from the past | Someone who lives very near Ella's school | A person who never speaks
exercise: «The distant past» means which? | Next week | *Long ago | Very near the front door | In the middle of the day
test: «Some parents are cool or distant: they say little and rarely praise or hug.» In this sentence distant means | *Not close or warm | Loudly singing | Far across the sea | Very tall
test: In a storm, «distant rumbles» are the sound of what? | *Thunder far away | Waves crashing on the beach | A train in the next street | A dog barking at the door
exam: In «the most distant object ever explored up close», what does distant mean? | Very small | Not friendly | Long ago | *Far away in space
